## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1 — Connection & Model Layer

#### [NEW] `connection.service.ts`
- **ConnectionProfile CRUD** — create, read, update, delete connection profiles
- **Health check** — test endpoint connectivity and list available models
- **Set default profile** — mark a profile as the default for new scenarios

#### [NEW] `llm-provider.service.ts`
- **Adapter pattern** — common interface (`LLMAdapter`) with methods: `complete(messages, options)`, `stream(messages, options)`, `listModels()`
- **OpenAI-compatible adapter** — works with OpenAI, Ollama, LM Studio, koboldcpp, text-generation-webui, any `/v1/chat/completions` endpoint
- **Streaming support** — SSE/fetch ReadableStream for token-by-token rendering
- **Prompt template system** — ChatML, Alpaca, Llama3, Mistral, Raw formats for prompt assembly

#### [MODIFY] `settings.page.ts`
- Add **LLM Connections** settings section — list profiles, create/edit/delete, test connectivity
- Add **Connection Editor** modal — endpoint URL, auth method, API key, model selection, sampling defaults, template selection

---

### Phase 5 — Standard Chat Engine

#### [NEW] `prompt-assembly.service.ts`
- **Prompt assembly pipeline** — builds the full prompt from: system instructions → active lore entries (via trigger scanning) → retrieved memories → recent message history
- **Token budget manager** — tracks token count, prioritizes context allocation
- **Lorebook trigger scanning** — scans recent messages for trigger words, injects matching entries

#### [MODIFY] `chat.page.ts` (major rewrite)
- **Full chat UI** — message list with bubbles (user/assistant/system/narrator roles), streaming token display
- **Message input** — text input with send button, character selector for group chats
- **Chat controls** — regenerate last response, edit messages, delete messages
- **Session management** — auto-save messages, update session title, link to scenario
- **Scenario "Start Chat" flow** — create a new ChatSession from a Scenario, route to chat page

#### [MODIFY] `scenario-editor.page.ts`
- Add **"Start Chat"** button to create a new session and navigate to the chat page

#### [MODIFY] `scenario-list.page.ts`
- Add **"Play"** button per scenario card to launch chat directly

